  "body": "Hi I raised this issue on golang but they suggested we fix this upstream here, whats your thoughts around support for still detecting 'text/html' when the leading tag is '<!--' but the next char is not a ' ', its a whitespace char (inclusive of '\\n' and '\\t' ?)\n\nI have a lot of html files that are incorrectly detected as 'text/plain' because i have an immediate '\\n' after the opening '<!--' tag. Golang team basically saying, they'll merge if you fix.\n\nThoughts?\n",
